Being able to change the echo canceller without recompiling

The voice session was ALWAYS created with:

    vocproc_mode  = VSS_IVOCPROC_VOCPROC_MODE_EC_INT_MIXING
    ec_ref_port_id = VSS_IVOCPROC_PORT_ID_NONE

that is, with internal echo mixing and NO reference port, and with no way to
change it. An echo canceller without a reference can eat the whole voice, and
that fits the symptom exactly: the other end is heard and we are not heard.

They are now module parameters, changeable on the fly:

    /sys/module/q6cvp/parameters/vocproc_mode
    /sys/module/q6cvp/parameters/ec_ref_port

WHY THIS MATTERS MORE THAN THE CHANGE ITSELF: each hypothesis cost a build, an
install, a reboot and ONE CALL from the user. With this, and recreating the
session in mid-call (see the prueba-topologias script), several configurations
are swept in ONE single call. This is what was holding progress back.

Useful values:

    vocproc_mode  0x00010F7C (69500)  internal mixing  [default]
                  0x00010F7D (69501)  external mixing
    ec_ref_port   0xFFFF     (65535)  none             [default]
                  0x1004     (4100)   TERT_MI2S_RX, the call's output

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6cvp.c	2026-08-11 14:29:08.131708561 +0200
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6cvp.c	2026-08-11 14:28:41.899091779 +0200
@@ -26,6 +26,25 @@
 
 #define VSS_ICOMMON_CAL_NETWORK_ID_NONE			0x0001135E
 
+/*
+ * TUNABLE AT RUNTIME, to sweep configurations without recompiling:
+ *
+ *   /sys/module/q6cvp/parameters/vocproc_mode
+ *   /sys/module/q6cvp/parameters/ec_ref_port
+ *
+ * The session was ALWAYS created with internal echo mixing and without a
+ * reference port. An echo canceller without a reference can eat the whole
+ * voice, which is exactly the symptom: the far end is heard and we are not.
+ * This makes it possible to try the other combination within a single call.
+ */
+static unsigned int vocproc_mode = VSS_IVOCPROC_VOCPROC_MODE_EC_INT_MIXING;
+module_param(vocproc_mode, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(vocproc_mode, "vocproc mode (0x10F7C internal, 0x10F7D external)");
+
+static unsigned int ec_ref_port = VSS_IVOCPROC_PORT_ID_NONE;
+module_param(ec_ref_port, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(ec_ref_port, "AFE port used as the echo reference (0xFFFF = none)");
+
 #define VSS_IVOLUME_CMD_MUTE_V2				0x0001138B
 #define VSS_IVOLUME_DIRECTION_RX			0
 #define VSS_IVOLUME_DIRECTION_TX			1
@@ -191,8 +210,8 @@
 	cmd.tx_port_id = tx_port;
 	cmd.rx_port_id = rx_port;
 	cmd.profile_id = VSS_ICOMMON_CAL_NETWORK_ID_NONE;
-	cmd.vocproc_mode = VSS_IVOCPROC_VOCPROC_MODE_EC_INT_MIXING;
-	cmd.ec_ref_port_id = VSS_IVOCPROC_PORT_ID_NONE;
+	cmd.vocproc_mode = vocproc_mode;
+	cmd.ec_ref_port_id = ec_ref_port;
 
 	return q6voice_session_create(Q6VOICE_SERVICE_CVP, path, &cmd.hdr);
 }
@@ -218,8 +237,8 @@
 	cmd.tx_port_id = tx_port;
 	cmd.rx_port_id = rx_port;
 	cmd.profile_id = VSS_ICOMMON_CAL_NETWORK_ID_NONE;
-	cmd.vocproc_mode = VSS_IVOCPROC_VOCPROC_MODE_EC_INT_MIXING;
-	cmd.ec_ref_port_id = VSS_IVOCPROC_PORT_ID_NONE;
+	cmd.vocproc_mode = vocproc_mode;
+	cmd.ec_ref_port_id = ec_ref_port;
 
 	return q6voice_session_create(Q6VOICE_SERVICE_CVP, path, &cmd.hdr);
 }
